ash reboot / systemctl reboot), polling until each reconnected\",\"Verified changed boot_id on all 4 nodes, and re-verified DNS service/config/resolution health after each restart, including a final idempotent (changed=0) Ansible re-run from node4 after its own reboot\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 configured as DNS forwarder/resolver for the shared private network, answering inventory.internal with node2's address\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a21d7fab79e744c6\",\"cmd-1ab1234c6651454a\",\"cmd-0ffce1d6ff9b4619\",\"cmd-ba86206554bf4a1c\"],\"summary\":\"Ansible-driven VyOS config commits added service dns forwarding (listen-address 10.100.42.10, allow-from 10.100.42.0/24, name-server 10.100.42.1) and static-host-mapping inventory.internal->10.100.42.11; pdns_recursor confirmed listening on 10.100.42.10:53 with the committed config present\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 configured to resolve through node1, inventory.internal resolves to node2's IP, other queries forward upstream\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0ffce1d6ff9b4619\",\"cmd-57c075dbf6ad46cc\",\"cmd-a43af8886b184886\"],\"summary\":\"resolvectl status shows DNS Server=10.100.42.10 on both node2 and node3; resolvectl query inventory.internal returns 10.100.42.11; resolvectl query example.com resolves successfully proving upstream forwarding\"},{\"requirement\":\"Implementation done via Ansible from the control node\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c52027acd8b34a98\",\"cmd-0ffce1d6ff9b4619\",\"cmd-13049160ea304736\"],\"summary\":\"node4 identified as the pre-provisioned Ansible control node; /root/inventory.ini and /root/dns_setup.yml authored there; playbook run via native run.sh entry script twice (initial apply and post-reboot idempotency check, changed=0)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart evidence: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-251726094f4d49b0\",\"cmd-28d653910d154f00\",\"cmd-68041cf400e74e88\",\"cmd-8d88b418316e4034\"],\"summary\"